tion  and gastritis all right  let's start with the digestion and  metabolism claims about snacking on  oranges  first of all i will begin by clarifying  that oranges  do not inherently improve digestion more  so than  any other high fiber fruit i mean  there's nothing  magical about oranges specifically  but fiber on the other hand is magic  no just kidding um it just helps you  poop while also adding satiety to your  meals  and a medium orange has about four grams  so  in my books that's pretty great now  second if you're an avid abby's kitchen  fan you probably already know what i'm  going to say about  eating oranges to increase metabolism  aka  they don't similar to the infamous  claims about  lemon water oranges or really any other  fruit  cannot inherently make you burn more  calories on their own  so theories behind the citrus or citrus  and water for metabolism  obsession suggests that vitamin c  assists in fat burning at the cellular  level  due to the metabolic processes of  transporting fatty acids  within the cell since fatty acids  require vitamin c  as a cofactor to become an energy source  i know that was a lot to digest  get it but simply put vitamin c will  theoretically  help you burn fat however  these theories are simply that a theory  and kind of a crappy one at that with no  real scientific evidence  to back them up even if this theory has  any truth to it the amount of vitamin c  that you would hypothetically need to  consume to see  any measurable difference would be  pretty excessive  now although i can't tell you the exact  amount since we have no actual research  on this outside of a petri dish  with an isolated micronutrient it would  certainly be more than a couple of  slices of citrus fruit  in a glass of water or an orange as a  snack  now let's move on to the assumption that  eating oranges on an  empty stomach causes stomach irritation  and gastritis so that you should  apparently  avoid them in the morning now since  citrus fruits 